  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN nodes rooted at node 111. The iii-th node has a label of AiA_iAi​.\n\nA node vvv is said to be in the **subtree** of uuu if the simple path from 111 to vvv passes through node uuu. We define SuS_uSu​ as the set of all nodes vvv such that v≠uv \\ne uv=u and vvv is in the subtree of uuu.\n\nA node uuu is said to be **good** if either of the following conditions hold:\n\n\nSuS_uSu​ is empty.\nSuS_uSu​ is non-empty, and let Su={X1,X2,....,XK}S_u = \\{X_1, X_2, ...., X_K\\}Su​={X1​,X2​,....,XK​}, then Au=AX1⊕AX2⊕…⊕AXKA_u = A_{X_1} \\oplus A_{X_2} \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus A_{X_K}Au​=AX1​​⊕AX2​​⊕…⊕AXK​​.\nA tree is **beautiful** iff all nodes are **good**.\n\nUnfortunately the given tree might not be beautiful already. In one operation, you can choose some node uuu and change it's value to any arbitrary non-negative integer. Let f(A)f(A)f(A) denote the minimum number of such changes to make the tree beautiful for the given array AAA.\n\nYou are given the tree of NNN nodes but not the array AAA. Calculate the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) for all (M+1)N(M + 1)^N(M+1)N arrays AAA satisfying the following constraints:\n\n\n∣A∣=N|A| = N∣A∣=N\n0≤Ai≤M0 \\le A_i \\le M0≤Ai​≤M\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of vertices and the upper bound on values.\nThe next N−1N - 1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th line contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤M≤9982443511 \\le M \\le 9982443511≤M≤998244351",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The set of input edges define a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
